# Auth and Permissions

## Session

1. Login: `POST /api/session/login` → backend `POST /auth/login` → set `httpOnly` cookies → return `{ user }` or `{ challenge }` for 2FA.
2. `middleware.ts`: refresh when access token is within 60s of expiry; on failure redirect `/login?next=<path>`.
3. Load `GET /auth/me` once on the server into a provider; refetch on window focus.
4. Idle timeout from `security-policy` settings: 60s warning, then logout.
5. Forced 2FA enrol blocks navigation until confirmed when policy requires it.

## Portal routing after login

| `userType` | Land on |
|---|---|
| `admin` (school management) | `/admin` |
| `staff` | `/staff` |
| `parent` | `/parent` |
| `student` | `/student` |

Also expose `/it` when the user has any of `system-update.*`, `backup.*`, `licensing.*`, `jobs.*` (or related IT permissions). Multi-portal users switch from the account menu.

Coarse middleware: `/parent/*` → parent, `/student/*` → student, `/it/*` → system permission. Fine checks stay in `<PermissionGate>` + backend.

## Permissions in UI

```tsx
// ✅
can('fees.invoice.create')
<PermissionGate permission="fees.invoice.create">...</PermissionGate>

// ❌ never
user.roles.includes('Bursar')
```

Prefer disabled button + tooltip when hiding an action would confuse the user. Menu items declare the permission they need. Out-of-scope ids → standard "not found or not available to you" page, never a raw error.
